  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Non-Food Items (NFI) and Lifesaving Shelter Assistance to Earthquake-Affected Households in T&#xfc;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The earthquake response in T&#xfc;rkiye is being lead and coordinated by the Disaster and Emergency Management Authority. A three-month state of emergency has been declared for eleven provinces that were directly affected by the earthquake. Around 3 million people, including migrants, are displaced in various settings including those choosing to stay close to their homes and others moving further away from their usual residence. An estimated 1.7 million people live in informal settlements, mostly in makeshift shelters or tents with extremely basic living conditions. Some of these settlements lack proper water and sanitation services and also require immediate assistance with basic household items and shelter support. 
 
In response to the immediate need for better shelter and access to basic services, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is improving access to basic services and temporary living conditions for populations affected by environmental hazards through the procurement and delivery of tents, living containers and essential housing items.</narrative>
  </description>
